From aa5f954bdef5f3359a8f0df7cfbcbbac114683de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hallel <hallel.kula@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 12:12:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dxf: terminate cquote's output at the last byte written

cquote() stores its NUL at d[len - 1], the last byte of the destination
buffer, and never at the position where it stopped writing.
dxf_fixup_string() then calls strlen() on that buffer, so every byte
between the end of the quoted string and the end of the allocation is
read back as string content.  The buffer is malloc'd with
(2 * emblen) + 1 bytes, so any string that grows by less than 2x under
quoting leaves such a gap.

Reproduces with the shipped test data, no allocator tricks needed:

  programs/dwg2dxf --as r2018 -y -o out.dxf test/test-data/example_2018.dwg
  grep -a Fgdt out.dxf

  expected   {\Fgdt;r}%%v1%%v2%%v%%v%%v^J10
  actual     {\Fgdt;r}%%v1%%v2%%v%%v%%v^J10v

The trailing byte is whatever the allocation happened to hold: the value
quotes to 30 bytes in a 59-byte buffer, and strlen() runs past the end of
what was written.  Same on example_2004, _2007, _2010 and _2013.  Under
MALLOC_PERTURB_ the residue grows to a long run rather than a single
byte, which is how it was first spotted.

This is the defect valgrind reported against MTEXT in 3c5ab3bb.  That
commit moved the buffer to a zeroed static, which changed the residue
from arbitrary heap to the previous call's tail rather than fixing the
termination; the buffer is malloc'd again today.

PR #1412

	* src/out_dxf.c (cquote): Terminate after the last byte written,
	clamped to the end of the buffer.
---
 src/out_dxf.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/out_dxf.c b/src/out_dxf.c
index c20d415468..4d8fbfacb1 100644
--- a/src/out_dxf.c
+++ b/src/out_dxf.c
@@ -1393,6 +1393,12 @@ cquote (char *restrict dest, const size_t len, const char *restrict src)
       else
         *dest++ = c;
     }
+  // Terminate after the LAST BYTE WRITTEN. Callers strlen() this buffer, so
+  // a NUL only at its end makes every byte the quoting did not reach part of
+  // the string -- uninitialized heap, for a buffer sized 2x the input.
+  if (dest >= dend)
+    dest = d + len - 1;
+  *dest = '\0';
   d[len - 1] = '\0'; // add final delim, skipped above
   return d;
 }
